+<details>
+<summary>FLUJO</summary>
+
+To attach an existing test browser over CDP from [FLUJO](https://flujo.com.co):
+
+1. Start a Chromium-family browser with remote debugging enabled and a separate test profile. Note its local CDP endpoint.
+2. In a working directory, run `npm install @playwright/mcp@latest`.
+3. In FLUJO, open **Connected Apps** > **Connect App** > **I'm an expert**. In **Configure & Test**, name the server `playwright` and set **MCP server root path** to that working directory.
+4. Select **Standard IO** and set **Run command** to `npx`. Add three separate **Arguments**: `-y`, `@playwright/mcp@latest`, and `--cdp-endpoint=http://127.0.0.1:9222` (replace the endpoint with your browser's).
+5. Click **3) Test run**, then **Add server** after the MCP handshake succeeds.
+6. Open the saved server's **Tools** tab. Test `browser_navigate` with a local test page URL, then `browser_snapshot` with its optional fields blank to display the accessibility snapshot in FLUJO.
+
+</details>
